Working on a tourist. A bit of change of pace from a
Samurai! Buck (XL9 AC-1) was rearranging the boulders on the
top floor of Sokoban when a green elf came round the corner
and fired off a /oSleep. Lucky Buck, that was one of three
intrinsic resistances acquired to date. Buck ran over and
started poking the elf with his long sword. After a few hits
while the elf was wasting charges on the wand (a Samurai
would have already killed him) the elf read a scroll and
there were 17 new monsters in view, and more I couldn't see
yet!

There was a tribe of Uruk-hai, about nine in full view, a
tribe of Mordor Orcs, about three in view, a large cat, a
small dog, a ghoul, a leprechaun and a homoculus. And of
course the elf was still with us and since they never travel
alone there had to be two or three more around the corner.

Buck did have the good fortune to have a tame large cat and
a tame large dog nearby. My first move was to tame the new
large cat, move two was to burn an Elbereth with my /oFire
to make a base. A long, dangerous battle ensued. Buck was
down to 36/92 a couple of times. A few poison arrows missed
(Yikes, no PR). A mumak, a lynx and a werewolf, another
ghoul, the other elves and the rest of the Mordor Orcs
joined in. I'm sure there were other I don't recall just
now. Whew!

I know we killed at least 25 monsters, mostly generated by
that scroll. I thought 17 was the max for a scroll but on
this and other occasions I've wondered if a tribe, like the
Uruk-hai in this case, counts as one of the 13 monsters
(1/73 you get 14 to 17).

BTW, is all jumping in Sokoban a luck penalty? Even if it
doesn't bypass a boulder? (One of Buck's escape choices).
